Subject: [PATCH] feat: Pin-Down alternate-angle scripts, competitor page
 audit, Leak Map benchmark-on-demand
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Verified all 4 previously-deferred "outside the box" Showtime ideas
against real code before building — 3 confirmed genuinely buildable, 1
confirmed NOT (kept declined, not built):

1. Pin-Down alternate-angle script regeneration: buildScriptPack already
   has a real, pre-modeled 3-way hero approach axis (research_assistance/
   urgency/faq, selectHeroApproach) — added approachOverride so an
   operator can force a specific one instead of the auto-picked one.
   Deliberately NOT a free-text "more aggressive" tone knob — there's no
   such parameter in the real prompt to hang that on.

2. Pin-Down competitor page audit: auditExistingConfirmationPage took
   exactly one URL. Added an optional second (competitor) URL, fetched
   the same way as the primary and folded into the same audit prompt as
   direct comparison context — degrades to the existing single-page audit
   if the competitor fetch fails, never fails the whole audit over it.

3. Leak Map benchmark-on-demand: getBenchmarkLines already exists as a
   plain, k-anonymized DB read the real audit pipeline calls internally.
   Exposed it standalone (compare_leak_map_benchmarks, an instant
   read-only chat tool, no dispatch/no LLM call) against a client's most
   recent already-computed audit metrics — no new audit run required.

4. Single-URL/page Leak Map audit: confirmed NOT buildable as described.
   AuditEngine.runAuditPipeline pulls account-wide booking/CRM metrics
   over a time window; there's no URL parameter anywhere in it, and
   there's no honest way to bolt one on without building an entirely
   different tool. Left alone.

All 3 wired through the full chat-skill path (event schema, dispatcher,
trigger functions, tool schemas, handler branches, system prompt) with
graceful degradation, not hard failures, when the optional inputs are
omitted.

